Patch 0090 (gen2_j -> build/gen2_k), 2026-11-26. Three default-off switches in CR_P0088, matched exactly ("all" does NOT enable them):
  jumpedge : a river jumper (Hog Rider, Royal Hogs, Ram Rider, Prince, ...) whose target is on its lane column, coming from the
             outer side more than BRIDGE_WALK_REACH off the column, jumps on a straight line to (target.x -+ 0.8, near bank + 1.5)
             = real (2.2 | 14.8, row 16.0). Inside JUMP_ZONE its speed scale is length / forward length (at most sqrt 2), so its
             forward speed is unchanged; then it runs straight ahead to far bank + 2.5 (engine 20 = real row 18) before it turns
             to its target. Beside the bridge (within BRIDGE_WALK_REACH of the column) or inside the walk corridor (arrival
             tolerance WAYPOINT_ARRIVAL_EPS) it takes the walker's waypoint instead of the 0087 jumpcol step onto the column.
  walklegs : a ground walker, like a jumper, spends the rest of its tick's step on the next leg after reaching a waypoint (up to
             3 legs), but only on a leg within about 18 degrees of the previous one (cos >= WALK_LEG_MIN_COS 0.95). Without it
             every waypoint cost the remainder of a step: about 4 % slow over the river. Without the angle rule two Goblin Machine
             bodies (0.75 + 0.75) at a bridge mouth turned the corner into the water every tick and stalled for ever (the
             "pairs of wide bodies cross the river" case in tests/core/test_board.cpp). Open-ground speed unchanged.
  hogspeed : the Hog Rider walks on land at 2.34 tiles/s (HOG_LAND_SPEED_OF_S50 0.975 x S/50; absolute, also without "speed");
             over the water (bank to bank, Troop::overWater) it keeps its own speed, so the jumpedge crossing is unchanged.
             Set in CardFactories::applyCardMetadata (Troop::landSpeedScale); no other card changes.
Measured on the live recordings (r5 detector, sprite bias removed), runs/bridge_1126:
  landing x real 2.2 / 14.8; gen2_j 2.57 / 14.43; gen2_k 2.20 / 14.80; timing unchanged (rows 17-21 within +0.05..-0.10 s).
  Walker river transit (real rows 14.5 -> 17.0, n 136): mean |sim - real| 0.14 s -> 0.08 s.
  Hog open ground past the river (speed2.py, real rows 18.6 -> 21.6, clean tracks): real 2.340 tiles/s (n 174, both screen
  halves, 95 % interval of the median 2.325-2.352) vs 2.40; same rows and mapping: Ice Golem 1.00, Skeletons 0.99-1.01 of S/50.
  Corner Hog sim - real at real row 20 / 22: -0.10 / -0.21 s -> -0.06 / -0.15 (left), -0.06 / -0.14 -> -0.03 / -0.09 (right).
Paths below start at engine/; apply from the build folder: cd build/gen2_X && patch -p1 < this. Also adds jumpedge/walklegs/
hogspeed to p0088_active() (src/bindings.cpp), python_ai/tests/test_bridge_crossing_0090.py (22; 16 fail on gen2_j), and makes
the 0087 cases of tests/core/test_board.cpp branch on P0088::jumpEdge() (plus one [patch0090] hogspeed case).
All three off = bit-identical to gen2_j (150 of 150 replays, per-tick log sha; runs/bridge_1126/verify).

